WEBVTT

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:16.230
Hi, toys. Bye, toys.

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:18.390
DOLLY: Jessie's back!

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:20.390
What's first grade like?
Tell me everything!

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:21.550
Well, it was...

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:22.630
How was "Present and Explain"?

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:24.350
Uh, you mean "Show and Tell"
there, big guy.

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:25.670
You see any kids eat paste?

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:26.750
JESSIE: Guys, listen!

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:29.350
Bonnie had a great day
in first grade.

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:31.710
She even made
a new friend in class.

00:00:31.790 --> 00:00:34.070
Oh, she's already
making friends.

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:36.830
No, no, she made a new friend.

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:39.710
Come on out, it's okay.

00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:45.350
(GASPING)

00:00:58.110 --> 00:01:01.510
Hi. I'm, uh... I'm Forky.

00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:03.670
(STUTTERS) Trash?

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:06.790
No, no. Toy.
I am a...

00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:08.990
We are all toys.

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:12.950
Unique, beautiful toys.

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:16.950
I will explain everything.

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:21.750
How am I alive?

00:01:24.110 --> 00:01:26.310
I don't know.

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:36.870
(CHORUS VOCALIZING)

00:01:41.630 --> 00:01:45.870
CHRIS STAPLETON: (SINGING)
I was a lonesome cowboy

00:01:47.150 --> 00:01:50.310
Lonesome as I could be

00:01:51.190 --> 00:01:55.150
You came along
and changed my life

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:58.750
And fixed
what was broken in me

00:02:00.230 --> 00:02:05.070
I was a lonesome cowboy

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:08.510
I didn't have a friend

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:13.790
Now I got friends
coming out of my ears

00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:17.630
I'll never be lonesome again

00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:23.030
You can't be happy
when you're all by yourself

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:25.470
Go on, tell me I'm wrong

00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:26.990
You're wrong

00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:31.350
When someone takes you
down from the shelf

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:34.790
And plays with you some
It's wonderful

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:36.230
Wonderful

00:02:36.390 --> 00:02:40.830
I was a lonesome cowboy

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:44.750
But not anymore

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:49.950
I just found out
What love is about

00:02:50.110 --> 00:02:53.350
I've never
felt this way before

00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:58.070
I was a lonesome cowboy

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:04.790
But not anymore

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:06.710
(CHORUS VOCALIZING)

00:07:46.230 --> 00:07:47.870
(MOTORCYCLE WHIRRING)

00:07:47.950 --> 00:07:50.590
(GRUNTING)

00:07:53.790 --> 00:07:54.910
Caboom!

00:07:56.390 --> 00:07:57.430
Yes!

